{"ts": 1791255216.063626, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=6] agent: You\u2019re stuck on the eval part, so here\u2019s the key distinction for Friday\u2019s build: **pass@k** means \u201cat least one of k runs succeeds,\u201d while **pass^k** means \u201call k runs succeed.\u201d For a build that needs reliable behavior, the writeup usually wants the stronger claim: repeated runs all work, not just one lucky success. If you want, I can help you turn that into a 2\u20133 sentence writeup statement.\n[t=6] student: hm ok", "t": 10, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.296727034588242, "pass_k": 0.37138563487761184}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6127447761339733, "motivation": 0.44783718433757524, "reliance": 0.3129446126246264, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
